  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape in mid-2026 is defined by the critical legislative progression of the CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633) onto the Senate Legislative Calendar, bringing the industry closer to structured regulatory definitions. In parallel, institutional Bitcoin adoption is moving beyond basic spot ETFs into programmatic corporate treasury reserves and sophisticated yield vehicles, like MSTR-backed bond ETFs. Technically, the industry continues to move away from highly vulnerable wrapped token bridges toward native, intent-based cross-chain liquidity networks. Meanwhile, the core architectural debate persists on the smart contract layer, where Bitcoin-native, decidable computational languages like Clarity challenge Ethereum's dominant but structurally vulnerable Turing-complete EVM by offering mathematically verifiable execution environments.",
